        "original_id": "d013e9e6-4761-5c53-b521-d10e25258215",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Maurice Elvey, Arthur Lubin\n- Works: Room in the House, Phantom of the Opera, Francis the Talking Mule, Mister Ed, Abbott & Costello films\n- Roles: Film directors, producer\n\nFacts:\n- Maurice Elvey was born on 11 November 1887 and died on 28 August 1967.\n- Arthur Lubin was born on July 25, 1898 and died on May 12, 1995.\n- Maurice Elvey was the most prolific film director in British history.\n- Arthur Lubin was an American film director and producer.\n- Arthur Lubin directed several Abbott & Costello films.\n- Arthur Lubin directed Phantom of the Opera in 1943.\n- Arthur Lubin directed the Francis the Talking Mule series.\n- Arthur Lubin created the talking-horse television series Mister Ed.\n- Room in the House is a 1955 comedy-drama film directed by Maurice Elvey.",
